# auth-robustness.test — adversarial cases for the login path (P5.8).
#
# Every case below is one of the failure modes that shipped to
# production in the 8CStudio audit or is a well-known auth failure
# from OWASP + published post-mortems. The pattern is:
#   1. Feed malformed stored credentials / cookies / tokens.
#   2. Assert graceful None / 401 / 400 — NEVER a 500 unhandled
#      exception in the most-public code path.
#
# Adopter customization:
#   - Wire `_call_login(email, password)` to your login endpoint.
#   - Wire `_set_stored_hash(user, hash_str)` to your user model / DB
#     helper (needed by the "malformed hash" cases).
#   - Skip cases that don't apply to your stack — but delete the skip,
#     don't leave a silent pass.

